{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy","id":1385661,"title":"The Essence of Virtue (Exalted: Essence's various new categories of Intimacy)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-04T14:51:05-07:00","id":1385661,"title":"The Essence of Virtue (Exalted: Essence's various new categories of Intimacy)","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1353035-exalted-essence?p=1378668#post1378668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence has a <b>Virtue </b>system. Virtues provide the umbrella under which Intimacies are defined. There are 7 Virtues. There are old Virtues and brand new ones. One of the Virtues is Ambition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Officially, Third Edition has only two categories for Intimacies: Principles and Ties.<br /> <br /> In practice, it has at least three, as Ties are always divided into positive and negative varieties. Even Principles could sometimes be divided in that way.<br /> <br /> Further, this minimal number of categories might have hindered imagination regarding the full range of possible Intimacies. Principles in particular could represent anything from personal goals, to life-style credos, to perceptions of reality...<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Ambition Intimacies&quot; could take the place of Principles which reflect goals you want to achieve in the world, and a general strength of Ambition would make it easier to form and keep Intimacies representing grand Ambitions.<br /> <br /> &quot;Prudence Intimacies&quot; could take the place of Principles which represent the character's interpretation of reality, such as their recollection of the past or their opinions on which economic and governmental principles actually work. The more Prudent a character is, the more they think about how the world works to anticipate future outcomes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fortitude / Temperance Intimacies&quot; could take the place of Principles which reflect the creeds by which you live, such as &quot;Honesty is the best policy&quot;. Again, the more Temperate or Fortified you are, the easier you find to structure your life according to strong principles, and to not waver from them.<br /> <br /> &quot;Compassion Intimacies&quot; could take the place of Ties, specifically positive Ties to people or beasts. The more Compassionate you are habitually, the easier you find it to care about other creatures in general, even when you've just met them, but especially if they're already big parts of your life.<br /> <br /> &quot;Passion/Lust Intimacies&quot; could take the place of positive Ties for objects and activities, reflecting a character's favorite possessions like manses or artifact weapons, and favorite pleasures like exploration, battle, gambling, sex, or food. The more lusty you are, the more you seek to enjoy life to the fullest.<br /> <br /> &quot;Conviction Intimacies&quot; could take the place of negative Ties in general. The Virtue of Conviction represents your rejection of everything you fear, and your commitment to avoiding or destroying those things you perceive as aberrations and detriments to the world, for the preservation of everything you care about (even if that's you and you alone).<br /> <br /> <br /> Alternatively, fear and hatred aren't backed by any Virtue at all, which would be an interesting commentary.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you think? What new Virtues do you think we might see, in addition to Ambition? Which of the old Virtues do you think should return?<br /> <br /> Do you think there are any sort of Intimacies which should not be grounded in or defined by any Virtue? Any sort of Intimacy which is simply antithetical to any kind of strength of character?<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I think one's Intimacy for one's self might be Virtue-agnostic. Self-love is the survival instinct, which even the least virtuous creature possesses in abundance. Even the self-love of the suicidal is easily aroused with a change in situation. Someone considering death through poison would suddenly fight for every breath if thrown into the ocean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T16:08:02-07:00","id":1385672,"title":"","content":"I think this has a potential to be vastly over-estimating what Virtues do in relaiton to INtimacies and I think it might be a better idea to like, wait to see what they are and how they work before setting ones' self up for what htings &quot;are gonna be&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 05-04-2020, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T17:03:50-07:00","id":1385686,"title":"","content":"This is interesting, but it honestly sounds rather complex for Essence. Essence is taking pains ensure that every Charm name gives a good indication of what the Charm is about, so I don't expect them to go with 7 types of Intimacies which you must read up and study to understand properly.<br /> <br /> Personally I expect the Virtues to simply be Intimacies for most intents and purposes. So the guy With a Major Virtue of Valor and a Minor Virtue of Ambition would more or less the same as someone in Ex3 who has a Major Principle of Valor and a Minor Principle of Ambition. Where things would differ is that those Virtues cannot be eroded normally, plus the fact that going against your Major Virtue is a Limit Trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T19:11:01-07:00","id":1385709,"title":"","content":"My theory is that virtues are mostly going to be around for virtue channels so that different characters can demonstrate a different approach to problems and the game can maintain a familiar maximum dice cap for Exalted without it being used for every single roll of consequence. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T20:23:10-07:00","id":1385721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385686#post1385686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is interesting, but it honestly sounds rather complex for Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I'm not the one who decided to bring Virtues back, and add three more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't expect them to go with 7 types of Intimacies which you must read up and study to understand properly. </div> </div> </div>And yet! That is exactly what we're told they're doing.<br /> <br /> All Intimacies will be defined according to 7 Virtues.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally I expect the Virtues to simply be Intimacies for most intents and purposes. So the guy With a Major Virtue of Valor and a Minor Virtue of Ambition would more or less the same as someone in Ex3 who has a Major Principle of Valor and a Minor Principle of Ambition. Where things would differ is that those Virtues cannot be eroded normally, plus the fact that going against your Major Virtue is a Limit Trigger. </div> </div> </div>How do you get any of that from the teaser?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T20:26:43-07:00","id":1385722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385709#post1385709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My theory is that virtues are mostly going to be around for virtue channels so that different characters can demonstrate a different approach to problems and the game can maintain a familiar maximum dice cap for Exalted without it being used for every single roll of consequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we might have Ambition points that can be channeled to supplement actions that align with Ambition-type Intimacies? Or to resist social influence opposed to such Intimacies?<br /> <br /> In that case, I hope these seven resource pools completely replace the Willpower trait and pool, because they'd be functionally the same, but sevenfold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T23:49:07-07:00","id":1385755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385686#post1385686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is interesting, but it honestly sounds rather complex for Essence...<br /> <br /> Personally I expect the Virtues to simply be Intimacies for most intents and purposes. So the guy With a Major Virtue of Valor and a Minor Virtue of Ambition would more or less the same as someone in Ex3 who has a Major Principle of Valor and a Minor Principle of Ambition. Where things would differ is that those Virtues cannot be eroded normally, plus the fact that going against your Major Virtue is a Limit Trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was pretty much my assumption. It would be a simplification, and that's what I expect from Essence.<br /> <br /> &quot;My character is really brave and quite ambitious,&quot; &quot;My character is really compassionate and quite self-controlled&quot;, etc.<br /> <br /> To go with, I assume, a simplified social system.*<br /> <br /> * So, willpower. Generally it's another cost for charms, and why bother having two different pools to pay for charms? Not to mention initiative, 1/blah with resets, etc. So why not just take it out? But the issue is the social system, which relies heavily on Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-05-2020, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T00:28:38-07:00","id":1385762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385721#post1385721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I'm not the one who decided to bring Virtues back, and add three more.</div> </div> </div> </div>No but you ARE the one who heard this little tidbit and, based on nothing BUT that decided to spin that out in a large direction and made a separate thread worrying about the implementation that you and only you thought up.<br /> <br /> Like... Chill. There's speculation and there's making a mountain out of a little bulge in the ground that MAY be a molehill eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T00:42:09-07:00","id":1385766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385721#post1385721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you get any of that from the teaser?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what teaser you're referring to, I'm just basing it on the following 2 Dev quotes from the Discord:<br /> <br /> &quot;Virtues are just Major and Minor, no dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Your Major Virtue is a potential Great Curse trigger, yes. (If you're a Solar, your Minor is too)&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385721#post1385721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Intimacies will be defined according to 7 Virtues.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the case then my guess is that a character's intimacies will be split into 3 : Those that fall under the Major Virtue, those that fall under the Minor Virtue, and then every other Intimacy.<br /> <br /> I'd also speculate that what does or doesn't qualify will not be locked in stone or mutually exclusive between Virtues. Helping a little girl find her lost cat might fall under one character's Conviction and another character's Compassion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 05-05-2020, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T01:05:38-07:00","id":1385770,"title":"","content":"So this is what the writers said:<br /> <br /> There are 7 Virtues. You have one Major and one Minor. (I didn't see that all 4 of the old ones are there though)<br /> They are the &quot;umbrella under which intimacies are defined&quot;.<br /> Intimacies still exist, they are only at Major or Minor (I assume because of being part of virtues).<br /> Virtues do not have a dot rating.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Monica is very pleased with the social system and how the above works.<br /> <br /> My assumption from this is that a character will look something like:<br /> Major - Temperance (vow of chastity, vow of poverty)<br /> Minor - Ambition (becoming head of the Abbey)<br /> <br /> And then the other things you care about fall under ordinary system resolution because your feelings aren't very strong. So while the above monk may not be very valourous (as that's not his Major or Minor virtue), he's brave enough that you still have to roll to scare him into fleeing.<br /> <br /> As there's no dot ratings, virtue channels seems unlikely to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T01:19:55-07:00","id":1385772,"title":"","content":"Hmmmmm....<br /> <br /> No, actually I'm not sure re-reading my assumption is correct. I still think there won't be virtue channels, but that doesn't seem like enough intimacies, as the Sidereal power given seemed to assume you'd have intimacies to the other PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T02:55:49-07:00","id":1385787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385721#post1385721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you get any of that from the teaser?</div> </div> </div> </div>There do be <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/onyx-path-publishing-announces-new-exalted-essence-corebook/\" target=\"_blank\">Other Sources of Information</a>.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385766#post1385766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what teaser you're referring to,</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is also <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com/exalted-essence-dev-team-interview\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told Podcast: Exalted Essence Dev Team Interview</a>. Maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:02:39-07:00","id":1385813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385762#post1385762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No but you ARE the one who heard this little tidbit and, based on nothing BUT that decided to spin that out in a large direction and made a separate thread worrying about the implementation that you and only you thought up.<br /> <br /> Like... Chill. There's speculation and there's making a mountain out of a little bulge in the ground that MAY be a molehill eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking, but all I hear is &quot;You're having BadWrong Fun. That is non-approved fun. Stop that.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are seven Virtues. All Intimacies will be defined by those Virtues. I'm not making that up. We can speculate about what Virtues would make sense within the context of &quot;all Intimacies can be divided among them somehow&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can contribute to this conversation, or you can simply not rain all over the parade.<br /> <br /> Because otherwise, you're doing nothing worthwhile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:06:39-07:00","id":1385814,"title":"","content":"Alright everyone, let's all relax a bit. It's just a game forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:14:27-07:00","id":1385819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy#post1385661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What new Virtues do you think we might see, in addition to Ambition? Which of the old Virtues do you think should return?</div> </div> </div> </div>Compassion, Valour and Temperance were all fine IMO. I think they'd work well if they're now more about social influence; even without virtue channels, while Compassion might well be a way for NPCs to convince you to help them, let them escape justice, etc, it's also a good defence against the bad guys influencing you to do something bad. (I'm not really sure what bad thing Temperance could be exploited to make you do, but I'm sure someone else can think of something)<br /> <br /> Conviction.... eh, I think it can be taken out.<br /> Firstly, it's about how strong your beliefs are, and what lengths you'll go to achieve those. Having Major/Minor Virtues and Intimacies already shows how strong they are; if my Dragonblood has a Major Ambition intimacy of &quot;rising to a high, well-paid position within his country, a Minor Valour intimacy of &quot;I don't fear the monsters of the desert&quot;, and that's his Virtues, then obviously he's less likely to give up on his ambition than he is to give up fighting a desert demon, and less likely to give up fighting a desert demon than he is to give up helping the poor (it's not that he doesn't wish them well, but there's so <i>many</i> of them, what can you do?).<br /> <br /> Secondly, Ambition seems a bit similar to Conviction honestly. A really ambitious character in 2nd ed would probably be Conviction-primary.<br /> <br /> Considering the classical-Mediterranean-meets-classical-Chinese influence of Exalted, I'd be tempted by the Greek virtues (Prudence/Wisdom, Justice, Temperance and Fortitude/Courage) or Confucian ones (humane behaviour, Justice, Propriety, Knowledge and Honesty), but honestly I don't think they all work well here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you think there are any sort of Intimacies which should not be grounded in or defined by any Virtue? Any sort of Intimacy which is simply antithetical to any kind of strength of character? </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you can fit them all in somewhere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I think one's Intimacy for one's self might be Virtue-agnostic. </div> </div> </div>I think, for most people, the game doesn't need to reflect their self-love via an Intimacy (unless the person is either self-loathing or exceptionally arrogant). Just rules like 3rd ed's &quot;you can't convince people to do something that negatively impacts themselves without a supporting major intimacy, or is extremely dangerous unless supported by a Defining Intimacy&quot; covers that.<br /> <br /> Also, I find that while theoretically players should probably have intimacies like &quot;murdering innocents is wrong&quot;, &quot;I value myself&quot; or even &quot;I want to live in a nice house&quot;, these are not things which players are generally going to write on their character sheets. It's probably easier to assume that, unless stated otherwise, most characters have at least a vague belief that murdering innocents is not okay, and certainly have at least a tiny bit of selfishness; that's the human condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-05-2020, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:16:27-07:00","id":1385820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385766#post1385766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what teaser you're referring to, I'm just basing it on the following 2 Dev quotes from the Discord:<br /> <br /> &quot;Virtues are just Major and Minor, no dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Your Major Virtue is a potential Great Curse trigger, yes. (If you're a Solar, your Minor is too)&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, that is ADDITIONAL information that in NO WAY contradicts what I said in the opening post.<br /> <br /> Even if each character can only have one Major and one Minor Virtue, there are still going to be SEVEN to choose from, and apparently all (or at least most) Intimacies must fall within one of those seven.<br /> <br /> So we can totally speculate about what Virtues would make the most sense as categories into which Intimacies might be divided.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your additional information also doesn't support your idea that Virtues and Intimacies will become the same thing, such that each character can only have two Intimacies. Because they would simply say that, rather than say &quot;all Intimacies will be defined by the seven Virtues&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Defined&quot; and &quot;replaced&quot; are extremely distinct things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that's the case then my guess is that a character's intimacies will be split into 3 : Those that fall under the Major Virtue, those that fall under the Minor Virtue, and then every other Intimacy. </div> </div> </div>Then you agree with me, but are talking like you don't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd also speculate that what does or doesn't qualify will not be locked in stone or mutually exclusive between Virtues. Helping a little girl find her lost cat might fall under one character's Conviction and another character's Compassion. </div> </div> </div>Nonsense.<br /> <br /> &quot;Helping a little girl find her lost cat&quot; is a goal; an Intimacy that exists until the task is complete, and then becomes irrelevant, like any other Ambitious goal. But in the meantime, it's harder to sway you from that path, even for the purpose of helping the little girl out in any other way.<br /> <br /> &quot;Little Girl (affection)&quot; is a compassion sentiment that can motivate one to help her find her cat, but that remains relevant even after that task is completed, and it actually makes you vulnerable to being swayed away from that task by influence to help the girl in other ways.<br /> <br /> &quot;Help those in need&quot; is a principle of conviction by which you live your life, and it can motivate you to help the girl, but it can also be used to sway you to do any number of other things that might help her or someone else entirely.<br /> <br /> <br /> What would be the point of having seven different Virtues if you could plug any Intimacy underneath any of them?<br /> <br /> What's so BadWrong about someone trying to have fun with other people in speculating about what those seven Virtues might be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:18:31-07:00","id":1385822,"title":"","content":"Edit: Nah, nevermind that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-05-2020, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:23:25-07:00","id":1385824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385722#post1385722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we might have Ambition points that can be channeled to supplement actions that align with Ambition-type Intimacies? Or to resist social influence opposed to such Intimacies?<br /> <br /> In that case, I hope these seven resource pools completely replace the Willpower trait and pool, because they'd be functionally the same, but sevenfold.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could live with virtue channels taking over the function of willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-05-2020, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:26:02-07:00","id":1385825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385772#post1385772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmmm....<br /> <br /> No, actually I'm not sure re-reading my assumption is correct. I still think there won't be virtue channels, but that doesn't seem like enough intimacies, as the Sidereal power given seemed to assume you'd have intimacies to the other PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree on both counts.<br /> <br /> I sure hope there won't be virtue channels. Willpower points would have fulfilled that function well enough in the past (since you couldn't channel a Virtue without them anyway) and they could do so in the future.<br /> <br /> Having seven different -- or even just two different -- Virtue channels would be redundant with Willpower points.<br /> <br /> Conversely, having only two Intimacies seems too few.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:29:21-07:00","id":1385826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385672#post1385672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this has a potential to be vastly over-estimating what Virtues do in relaiton to INtimacies and I think it might be a better idea to like, wait to see what they are and how they work before setting ones' self up for what htings &quot;are gonna be&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speculation is healthy especially in a time where some of us are going a little stir crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:31:00-07:00","id":1385828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385826#post1385826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speculation is healthy especially in a time where some of us are going a little stir crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right? It's almost like we're in the middle of a GLOBAL LOCKDOWN.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385824#post1385824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could like with virtue channels taking over the function of willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>With a Major and Minor Virtue for each character, wouldn't that be merely replacing Willpower with at least two different forms of Willpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:45:10-07:00","id":1385831,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping PCs will only have one resource to keep track of (which I guess would be Motes). Not having Willpower would require major changes to the social system, and how it interacts with other parts of the game though.*<br /> Either way, I'd prefer Major Virtues giving +2/-2 Resolve or whatever to giving a resource that can be spent to ignore social influence. Though I guess, in practice, it might be fine.<br /> <br /> *Saying this... the thing with Ex3 social influence is that, most of the time, you can spend WP to resist. Which is awkward, because you might need that for combat charms. Resisting the social system does weaken you in other ways, so a PC's &quot;success&quot; at social influence should then help the group in combat or whatever, even if they didn't persuade the bad guy to stop his evil plan.<br /> <br /> But I think in practice social characters do sometimes feel that if an NPC spends WP, they've basically just failed, because it's unlikely to WP-tap that NPC anyway; either they'll recover it by next time the PCs meet, or there'll be a fight but NPCs don't normally spend all their WP in fights anyway so it'll make no difference.<br /> Of course, I don't really want the social character to be able to talk down every NPC because then the combat characters don't get to do anything. Not sure how to square that circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:53:28-07:00","id":1385834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385819#post1385819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compassion, Valour and Temperance were all fine IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can easily imagine Compassion Intimacies and Temperance Intimacies, as I explained in the original post.<br /> <br /> I excluded Valor for a reason. I don't see what kind of Intimacies it could support that wouldn't be better defined by Ambition or Lust/Passion.<br /> <br /> It definitely wouldn't be the Virtue for &quot;things I want to destroy&quot;, because that's fear, and Valor is practically the opposite of fear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not really sure what bad thing Temperance could be exploited to make you do, but I'm sure someone else can think of something </div> </div> </div>Old Temperance was only useful for NOT doing things, but it didn't actually motivate you to DO anything.<br /> <br /> But as I explained, Temperance Intimacies could replace Principles representing the creeds by which you live. And people can motivate you to do things that align with your creeds. If you live your life by the stricture that &quot;Honesty is the best policy&quot;, you can be convinced to spill your secrets, or to blow the lid off of your ally's conspiracy. If you live with the credo that &quot;Alcohol is a poison&quot;, you can be convinced to pick a fight with someone who is drinking heavily but otherwise minding their business.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conviction.... eh, I think it can be taken out. </div> </div> </div>Can you think of a better Virtue for fears than Conviction? Perhaps &quot;Justice&quot;, but would the name be any more appropriate for the concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T09:16:12-07:00","id":1385848,"title":"","content":"I honestly think that Intimacies of fear, including hatred, might be literally Virtueless Intimacies.<br /> <br /> Do such sentiments ever arise out of any strength of character? Are they ever more than hindrances?<br /> <br /> Opposing evil can instead be motivated by good. I fight and kill a beast not because I hate it, but because I love the home it threatens. My love is constructive and Virtuous, but pure fear for the monster itself would only be destructive and Vicious.<br /> <br /> Fear or hatred for fear's sake alone would be more like a scar, self-inflicted through bad choices or imposed upon you by others who seek to bring you down or control you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-05-2020, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T11:33:28-07:00","id":1385879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385831#post1385831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping PCs will only have one resource to keep track of (which I guess would be Motes). Not having Willpower would require major changes to the social system, and how it interacts with other parts of the game though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer if Willpower was the ONLY &quot;energy&quot; resource, and that the simplified, universalized Charmset relied on other methods to prevent you from using all of your Charms on the same turn, and from using your best Charms every turn.<br /> <br /> We have Willpower points, health levels, Initiative points, reset conditions, and the ability to design Charms that are either mutually exclusive when they do supplement similar actions or else supplement mutually exclusive actions.<br /> <br /> Anima levels could be something you ramp up voluntarily; one level each turn -- for Dragon-Blooded, they have to worry about collateral damage, and Celestials have to worry about exposure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T11:51:14-07:00","id":1385885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385879#post1385879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer if Willpower was the ONLY &quot;energy&quot; resource, and that the simplified, universalized Charmset relied on other methods to prevent you from using all of your Charms on the same turn, and from using your best Charms every turn.<br /> <br /> We have Willpower points, health levels, Initiative points, reset conditions, and the ability to design Charms that are either mutually exclusive when they do supplement similar actions or else supplement mutually exclusive actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be fine with that, but Motes are in. And I think you get less than 3rd ed (maybe significantly less) but more than Godbound's Effort (which I think is like 5-10? Not played Godbound).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T12:29:04-07:00","id":1385893,"title":"","content":"What about fear-based Intimacies? Do you see them as potentially Virtuous in some way, or to essentially treat all fear as something like a derangement?<br /> <br /> <br /> After all, is not fear the Mind-Killer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-05-2020, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:13:07-07:00","id":1385910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385762#post1385762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No but you ARE the one who heard this little tidbit and, based on nothing BUT that decided to spin that out in a large direction and made a separate thread worrying about the implementation that you and only you thought up.<br /> <br /> Like... Chill. There's speculation and there's making a mountain out of a little bulge in the ground that MAY be a molehill eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leave the tone policing to the mods, please. Thanks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:31:30-07:00","id":1385917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385893#post1385893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about fear-based Intimacies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was thinking about this. I've not really seen any PCs with fear-based intimacies (probably because it seems like purely a weakness). But of course, intimidation in 3rd ed is often an Instill action to Instill an intimacy of fear. Maybe it's not in Essence. Or maybe it is!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T14:39:51-07:00","id":1385942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385917#post1385917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was thinking about this. I've not really seen any PCs with fear-based intimacies (probably because it seems like purely a weakness). But of course, intimidation in 3rd ed is often an Instill action to Instill an intimacy of fear. Maybe it's not in Essence. Or maybe it is!</div> </div> </div> </div>Fear strong enough to be its own Intimacy IS a weakness, I agree. The line between it and a Phobia seems thin.<br /> <br /> Fear that strong cripples a character's reasoning and will-to-action. People who give into fear that much are making a mistake. People who seek to inspire that level of fear in others do so to cripple their self-control and rationality.<br /> <br /> Fear is the mind-killer, and hatred is the child of fear. I think it would make a strong, edifying statement if such Intimacies are truly Virtueless. It's personal suffering that leads to the misery of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T14:50:50-07:00","id":1385946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385820#post1385820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, that is ADDITIONAL information that in NO WAY contradicts what I said in the opening post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to prove that you're wrong? I posted my own speculation and you asked what I was basing it on, so I gave you the 2 quotes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385820#post1385820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if each character can only have one Major and one Minor Virtue, there are still going to be SEVEN to choose from, and apparently all (or at least most) Intimacies must fall within one of those seven.<br /> <br /> So we can totally speculate about what Virtues would make the most sense as categories into which Intimacies might be divided.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your additional information also doesn't support your idea that Virtues and Intimacies will become the same thing, such that each character can only have two Intimacies. Because they would simply say that, rather than say &quot;all Intimacies will be defined by the seven Virtues&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Defined&quot; and &quot;replaced&quot; are extremely distinct things.</div> </div> </div> </div> My idea was more that the 2 virtues would be 2 special intimacies among all your intimacies, not that they would be the only 2 you would have. I don't have the quote that says all intimacies will be defined by virtues, so it's hard for me to comment on that part.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385820#post1385820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you agree with me, but are talking like you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm actively trying to work with you here. Again, I'm not trying to prove you wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385820#post1385820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonsense.<br /> <br /> &quot;Helping a little girl find her lost cat&quot; is a goal; an Intimacy that exists until the task is complete, and then becomes irrelevant, like any other Ambitious goal. But in the meantime, it's harder to sway you from that path, even for the purpose of helping the little girl out in any other way.<br /> <br /> &quot;Little Girl (affection)&quot; is a compassion sentiment that can motivate one to help her find her cat, but that remains relevant even after that task is completed, and it actually makes you vulnerable to being swayed away from that task by influence to help the girl in other ways.<br /> <br /> &quot;Help those in need&quot; is a principle of conviction by which you live your life, and it can motivate you to help the girl, but it can also be used to sway you to do any number of other things that might help her or someone else entirely.<br /> <br /> <br /> What would be the point of having seven different Virtues if you could plug any Intimacy underneath any of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well common sense is still expected of the players. I think &quot;Help those in need&quot; might make a fine Principle of Compassion, but not so much of Lust.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385820#post1385820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's so BadWrong about someone trying to have fun with other people in speculating about what those seven Virtues might be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to do exactly that (have fun with other people speculating). I apologize if my original comment that your theory sounded complex for Essence came off as dismissive, that was not the intent. I'd really appreciate if you could drop the confrontational tone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 05-05-2020, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T15:32:18-07:00","id":1385952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385946#post1385946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize if my original comment that your theory sounded complex for Essence came off as dismissive, that was not the intent. I'd really appreciate if you could drop the confrontational tone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blaque's thread-crapping post right before your post might have led me to misinterpret your intent. If so, I apologize.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your idea of Virtues acting as some kind of super-Intimacy makes some kind of sense. If you choose Compassion as your Major Virtue, obviously you're a very compassionate person in general without need for multiple Intimacies to reflect that, whereas if Ambition isn't even your Minor Virtue, you would obviously be ambitious only about a few highly-specific things.<br /> <br /> But those few, highly specific things would still classified as Ambition Intimacies for the purposes of Charms that seek to instill, erode, or otherwise play off of ambitious specifically, as opposed to other sorts of intimacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T15:36:02-07:00","id":1385953,"title":"","content":"Right, I was a bit much on my initial post, and for that I apologize.<br /> <br /> Now, something productive, something productive.<br /> <br /> So seven Virtues. Ambition is allegedly one of the new ones. And presuming that the Classic Four are returning, which one would I add...<br /> <br /> I like the idea of some kind of Duty as a Virtue, separate from Compassion in that Duty is what you feel is the Greater Good for everyone rather than how I'd classify Compassion as the Personal Caring. Granted some of that may be due to drift with Scion 2e, where each Pantheon has two Virtues and they sometimes come into conflict and that's where the Drama happens.<br /> <br /> The Hindu Deva, in particular, have their Virtues as Duty and Conscience, which can best be described as &quot;What Society Says Is Right&quot; (Duty) vs &quot;What You Say Is Right&quot; (Conscience).<br /> <br /> So yeah, there may be room for some kind of Wider-Spread &quot;For The Greater Good/Needs of the Many&quot; view, along with making Compassion the &quot;Caring about the small things&quot; view.<br /> <br /> Granted the problem with this is that Duty may overlap with Conviction, assuming Conviction returns.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T15:48:23-07:00","id":1385955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385953#post1385953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, I was a bit much on my initial post, and for that I apologize.<br /> <br /> Now, something productive, something productive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apology accepted, glad to have a civilized conversation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So seven Virtues. Ambition is allegedly one of the new ones. And presuming that the Classic Four are returning, which one would I add... </div> </div> </div>We don't know for a fact that all of the original four are returning.<br /> <br /> I can see cases for everything but Valor. Not only is Valor very close to Ambition, I can think of countless Ambitious Intimacies and not a single Valorous Intimacy.<br /> <br /> Ambition is expressed with specific goals, each of which is a specific ambition that can be represented as individual Intimacies.<br /> <br /> But Valor is a singular impulse of &quot;I am in charge&quot; with no real room for such nuance.<br /> <br /> My proposed &quot;Passion / Lust&quot; Virtue can include bloodthirst, the craving for adrenaline, a love for competition, or the thrill of battle, in addition to more peaceful pursuits like music, fine wine, drugs, exotic foods, exploring new locations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Granted the problem with this is that Duty may overlap with Conviction, assuming Conviction returns. </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that in Third Edition, Principles can not only cover personal standards of behavior, but also Beliefs. Either beliefs regarding one's memories of the past, or belief in one's perception of the world around one.<br /> <br /> A capitalist has a Principle of &quot;People cannot achieve prosperity without personal property rights&quot; while a communist has a Principle of &quot;People cannot achieve prosperity when anyone has personal property rights&quot;.<br /> <br /> These could possibly be Prudence Intimacies, since Prudence is the virtue of &quot;Wisdom&quot; or &quot;Right Reason&quot;. The act of examining the world, reflecting on one's experiences, and gathering empirical data to attempt to arrive at a clear view of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T15:49:47-07:00","id":1385956,"title":"","content":"I could see Duty.<br /> <br /> But with that and Ambition, and Major/Minor intimacies, I definitely don't think Conviction would be necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T16:20:12-07:00","id":1385964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385955#post1385955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't know for a fact that all of the original four are returning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually we have the following quote talking about Virtues :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monica, Exalted Essence Chef</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You will recognize the classic ones in new, more usable forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the original 4 seem to be returning with some adjustments (probably to help with the sort of issues you pointed out). So maybe Valor will now be called Courage or something so it's easier to understand what Intimacies fall under it, but it should still be there in one form or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T16:21:36-07:00","id":1385966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385955#post1385955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't know for a fact that all of the original four are returning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean there's a reason I said PRESUMING, not &quot;And we know that the old Virtues are returning&quot;<br /> <br /> I also figure that if it's keeping Ties and Principles, it will be like...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Major Virtue</b>: Compassion<br /> <i>Principle</i>: Everyone deserves a fair education<br /> <i>Principle</i>: Nobody should go hungry<br /> <i>Tie</i>: My Bondmate (BrOTP)<br /> <br /> <b>Minor Virtue:</b> Ambition<br /> <i>Principle:</i> The world ain't gonna fix itself </div> </div> </div>And then perhaps a smattering of others that don't fall under your Major and Minor Virtues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T16:37:51-07:00","id":1385972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385964#post1385964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually we have the following quote talking about Virtues</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay then.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the original 4 seem to be returning with some adjustments (probably to help with the sort of issues you pointed out). So maybe Valor will now be called Courage or something so it's easier to understand what Intimacies fall under it, but it should still be there in one form or another. </div> </div> </div>We already have Courage. It is called Willpower; the power to overcome fear, whereas Valor was confidence enough to avoid feeling fear in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> I suppose one could break Valor into different AREAS of confidence. &quot;I am unbeatable with a sword&quot; versus &quot;I am unbeatable at chess&quot; or &quot;I can seduce any man&quot;.<br /> <br /> One who chooses Valor as their Major Virtue might be overbearingly confident at their ability to overcome any kind of adversity, regardless of their actual skill. Someone like the Moonsilver Caste Alchemical, <i>Excessively Righteous Blade</i>, who was always getting into trouble beyond his ability because he always overestimated himself and never turned down a challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T17:20:28-07:00","id":1385977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385966#post1385966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also figure that if it's keeping Ties and Principles</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, since I asked Neall if those were sticking around, and he avoided the question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also figure that if it's keeping Ties and Principles, it will be like... </div> </div> </div>I think it would look like this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>BAKUGOU KATSUKI</u><br /> Major Virtue: Valor<br /> Minor Virtue: Ambition<br /> Intimacies: (Compassion) &quot;Kirishima is okay&quot;, (Temperance) &quot;Work hard, study hard, and keep a clean record&quot;<br /> Fears: &quot;Being Looked Down On&quot;<br /> <br /> Bakugou is overwhelmingly confident and ambitious, to the point that he perhaps doesn't need specific Intimacies so much as &quot;super-Intimacies&quot; as potentially represented by his pair of Major and Minor Virtues.<br /> <br /> His other Virtues are so much weaker that they can be represented by specific Intimacies in the areas he actually cares about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-05-2020, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T22:21:37-07:00","id":1386006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1385972#post1385972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already have Courage. It is called Willpower; the power to overcome fear, whereas Valor was confidence enough to avoid feeling fear in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we know Willpower's going to be in Essence? I mean I wouldn't miss it if it was abandoned on the roadside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T22:26:02-07:00","id":1386009,"title":"","content":"I don't think any confirmation on either but I doubt they would completely remove it, even if they are just simplifying. May simplify what it can do, maybe not allow stunts to give you them. Not sure","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T03:08:42-07:00","id":1386030,"title":"","content":"It's not been mentioned at all.<br /> <br /> I hope they take it out. It's another thing to keep track of, a holdover from WoD; if you've only got 10 or so motes it seems superfluous. But... as I said before, taking it out would require big changes to the social system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T08:16:14-07:00","id":1386083,"title":"","content":"As I've said, I consider Willpower more important than Motes, and wouldn't mind seeing Motes disappear.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, the holistic theory I like so far:<br /> <br /> Fear and hatred are Virtueless, and are closer to flaws than Intimacies.<br /> <br /> Choosing a Virtue as your Major or Minor basically gives you that Virtue as a super-broad Intimacy, and your other Intimacies reflect specific areas you actually care about within the other five Virtues.<br /> <br /> Someone who chooses Compassion as one of their Virtues is that all-loving sort of character who strives to save everyone, even their antagonists. Aang the Avatar, as an example, or the man that Uncle Iroh became before the show began. But someone who doesn't choose Compassion for their pair can only really be motivated or stirred if they care about someone in particular. Toph cared very little for people in general, except for the friends she made along the way.<br /> <br /> Valor could represent confidence. Someone who chooses Valor as one of their Virtues is confident that they can meet and defeat any challenge, even in areas where that confidence might not be warranted. Azula is a good example of someone utterly convinced of her superiority and her ability to succeed; even if confronted in an area of weakness, she wouldn't balk but instead immediately look for a way to change the game in her favor. Meanwhile, Aang was confident in his ability to defend himself and escape from danger and in his ability to make friends, but he lacked the confidence to assert himself in his Earthbending training with Toph. Zuko never showed a lack of confidence in his ability to ninja-sneak his way into or out of any situation, but Azula knew all of the areas where he lacked confidence and struck him there. Katara didn't start as a very confident person in general, but over the course of time she developed confidence in her abilities as she mastered them.<br /> <br /> Temperance could still represent self-control, with a Major or Minor acting much like the Virtue did before, give or take some adjustment. Someone who isn't Temperate in all things can choose specific Intimacies for the principles their character is most passionate about keeping: No Lying, No Intoxicants Ever, Vow of Chastity/Monogamy, Vow of Celibacy, Pay Back All Debts.<br /> <br /> Conviction needs the most work, given its frequent interpretation as the &quot;do what I want&quot; Virtue.<br /> <br /> <br /> My proposed Passion/Lust Virtue, taken as Major or Minor, would represent someone with a relentless curiosity and &quot;joy of life&quot;. It's not that they must overindulge in anything, but they're always down to try anything at least once, and they live in a perpetual state of wanderlust. They can almost always see the bright side of almost anything, finding fun and humor in whatever they're doing... whether they have the compassion to use that to raise others' spirits, or whether they're a sadist who uses their joy to twist the knife on others' suffering.<br /> <br /> <br /> If Ambition represents driving goals, it is easy to envision in terms of individual and specific goals, but as a whole Virtue, what would Ambition look like?<br /> <br /> Would it represent a desire to achieve as much control over the world as possible, in general? Such a broad goal would definitely seem out of place as a single Intimacy for someone who didn't choose Ambition as Major or Minor.<br /> <br /> But as a super-Intimacy of &quot;Take Over The World&quot;, it doesn't provide nuance to lesser goals. I could persuade someone with a goal of &quot;Reform The Scarlet Empire&quot; to help me if I convince them doing so would further their own goal, but someone with Ambition as their Major Virtue may prefer the Scarlet Empire as it is... just with them in charge. Or they do want to change it after they take control. Either way, the distinction would seem to require a specific Ambition Intimacy despite having the all-encompassing super-Intimacy.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, someone who wants to Rule The World derives their opinions on whether or not the Scarlet Empire needs reforming based on other Virtues. If they paired Compassion with Ambition, they would naturally want to reform the Scarlet Empire. But without sufficient Compassion, they probably don't care about anything but gaining and maintaining control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-06-2020, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:33:16-07:00","id":1386112,"title":"","content":"Taking a &quot;from the hip&quot; response here, is the idea of the 7 categories as a way of simplifying what Intimacies are (as Sunder says above), and how they can be manipulated? If someone has the Compassion virtue/intimacy, that would represent something that can be used in a persuade action or similar. Major vs Minor functions as a level, as before.<br /> <br /> It's not as nuanced as the Intimacies system, but it's not meant to be. It's a broad generalisation of the system, that would facilitate a similar sort of social system to the main game without having to keep track of umpteen intimacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T12:05:28-07:00","id":1386138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386112#post1386112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking a &quot;from the hip&quot; response here, is the idea of the 7 categories as a way of simplifying what Intimacies are (as Sunder says above), and how they can be manipulated? If someone has the Compassion virtue/intimacy, that would represent something that can be used in a persuade action or similar. Major vs Minor functions as a level, as before.<br /> <br /> It's not as nuanced as the Intimacies system, but it's not meant to be. It's a broad generalisation of the system, that would facilitate a similar sort of social system to the main game without having to keep track of umpteen intimacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're going from three or four categories of Intimacy to seven, and adding the choice of Major and Minor Virues which might be something other than Super-Intimacies.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where you see things becoming simpler.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like, if you wanted to play an all-loving hero, instead of it choosing Compassion to serve as a Super-Intimacy, wouldn't it be enough to have a Defining positive Tie of &quot;Everyone (all-encompassing love)?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T12:05:30-07:00","id":1386139,"title":"","content":"My assumption is that this is supposed somehow to make things simpler. I can't imagine they'd make it more complicated. But I don't know how 7 Virtues does make it simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T12:13:49-07:00","id":1386143,"title":"","content":"I assume that, instead of tracking each named intimacy, you just track whether or not each of the Virtues applies. Cuts down on the amount of bookkeeping intimacies requires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:00:55-07:00","id":1386152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386143#post1386143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that, instead of tracking each named intimacy, you just track whether or not each of the Virtues applies. Cuts down on the amount of bookkeeping intimacies requires.</div> </div> </div> </div>But each character only has two Virtues, Major and Minor.<br /> <br /> Just two Intimacies is a bit lean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:03:26-07:00","id":1386154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386143#post1386143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that, instead of tracking each named intimacy, you just track whether or not each of the Virtues applies. Cuts down on the amount of bookkeeping intimacies requires.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought, but then why have Intimacies at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T13:39:29-07:00","id":1386166,"title":"","content":"Here's a new tidbit from the Discord, though it can be interpreted in any number of ways:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Discord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Discord Member:</b> So, do you pick one Major and one Minor intimacy out of the 7(?) new intimacies?<br /> <br /> <b>Dev1:</b> You pick a Major and Minor of the 7 yes<br /> <br /> <b>Dev1:</b> They're like guideposts for roleplay and writing your Intimacies<br /> <br /> <b>Dev2:</b> They also plug into the social system</i></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T16:00:43-07:00","id":1386199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386166#post1386166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a new tidbit from the Discord, though it can be interpreted in any number of ways:</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to confirm that the seven Virtues do not replace Intimacies, not even the two Virtues you choose.<br /> <br /> So, no Super-Intimacies in the sense that, if I choose Compassion as my Major Virtue, that would make it redundant and pointless to have any Compassion-based Intimacies.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, that eliminates my concern about what the super-Intimacies of Conviction and Ambition would be like, since that's not what you get for choosing either as Major or Minor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:51:49-07:00","id":1386323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386199#post1386199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems to confirm that the seven Virtues do not replace Intimacies, not even the two Virtues you choose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed.<br /> <br /> It does seem odd to me to add another level in, which would seem to make it<i> more </i>complex, but maybe in practice it doesn't. And there might be an element of guiding intimacies because the writers think new players might find it hard to think of them?<br /> <br /> (Personally, I don't find that players can't think of intimacies per-se, but I do find that some think of tons and others can only think of 2 or 3. But then, I'm not sure that PCs need more than 6 or 7, as long as it includes the other PCs.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T12:30:22-07:00","id":1386450,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone has really agreed with me or challenged me on the idea that Intimacies of fear and hatred might be Virtueless.<br /> <br /> Can anyone think of a Virtue that would make you more fearful or hateful in a positive, advantageous way?<br /> <br /> Or does a &quot;Virtue&quot; of fear and hatred sound more like a disadvantage and a character flaw that gets your character into trouble in return for experience points?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T12:47:46-07:00","id":1386463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386450#post1386450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone has really agreed with me or challenged me on the idea that Intimacies of fear and hatred might be Virtueless.<br /> <br /> Can anyone think of a Virtue that would make you more fearful or hateful in a positive, advantageous way?<br /> <br /> Or does a &quot;Virtue&quot; of fear and hatred sound more like a disadvantage and a character flaw that gets your character into trouble in return for experience points?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see fear and hatred more as motivations behind a virtue.<br /> <br /> -Your fear the Tyrant will punish dissent by hurting innocents, so you cultivate the temperance not to challenge him until the time is right.<br /> <br /> -You fear the immense guilt of others telling you how you could have helped them and prevented all their suffering, so you become compassionate.<br /> <br /> -You fear looking weak, so you stand valorously against the Dark Lord's armies rather than fleeing.<br /> <br /> etc.<br /> <br /> Alternatively<br /> <br /> -Your burning hatred for the Tyrant will not let him get away with anything short of destroying everything he holds dear, so you bide your time with temperance.<br /> <br /> -Your hatred of the corrupted monks who raised you pushes you to be nothing like them, making you strive to be compassionate.<br /> <br /> -Your hatred of the Dark Lord pushes you to make a valorous stand against his armies even though your instincts would tell you to flee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T13:20:00-07:00","id":1386469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386463#post1386463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see fear and hatred more as motivations behind a virtue.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not something associated with or defined by a specific Virtue?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -You fear the Tyrant will punish dissent by hurting innocents, so you cultivate the temperance not to challenge him until the time is right. </div> </div> </div>I feel &quot;fear&quot; of this level is merely &quot;concern&quot; and doesn't merit a even minor Intimacy of fear for the Tyrant.<br /> <br /> It's enough to have an Intimacy representing your care for the innocents, and for your character to know that provoking the Tyrant will result in him making them suffer.<br /> <br /> You COULD have a personal fear of the Tyrant, and your COULD have a persistent fear that your actions will doom others to suffer. But neither of those Intimacies would be necessary, and both would be Vicious extremes rather than Virtuous. They would be wounds and flaws to overcome, rather than strengths to cultivate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -You fear the immense guilt of others telling you how you could have helped them and prevented all their suffering, so you become compassionate. </div> </div> </div>I can definitely see such a fear, strong enough to be an Intimacy or even a Derangement, coexisting with a Major Virtue of Compassion.<br /> <br /> But the fear would still be a mental illness that the character could overcome without replacing Compassion as their Major Virtue, because one wouldn't need such a fear to choose to be so Compassionate in the first place.<br /> <br /> Likewise with your Valor example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Your burning hatred for the Tyrant will not let him get away with anything short of destroying everything he holds dear, so you bide your time with temperance. </div> </div> </div>Co-existence doesn't mean correlation. You could hate him just as much without any Temperance. Temperance doesn't mean hating him more, though your hatred could motivate you to be less Temperate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Your hatred of the corrupted monks who raised you pushes you to be nothing like them, making you strive to be compassionate.<br /> <br /> -Your hatred of the Dark Lord pushes you to make a valorous stand against his armies even though your instincts would tell you to flee. </div> </div> </div>My response is the same as for the fear examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T15:09:29-07:00","id":1386509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386469#post1386469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But not something associated with or defined by a specific Virtue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. You have a virtueless intimacy of &quot;Tyrant (Hatred)&quot;, which pushes you to adopt the virtuous principle &quot;(Temperance) I will strike the Tyrant when the time is right&quot;. Your hatred pushed you to become more virtuous, but it is not the virtue itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386469#post1386469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>snip</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree with your comments, I don't think fear or hatred is necessary for any of the 7 Virtues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:00:04-07:00","id":1386521,"title":"","content":"I mean if you have Compassion as your Major Virtue then I think it would be logical to have a negative Intimacy towards a cruel tyrant that abuses your people. I dunno if Fear is needed as one of the big Virtues.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, one could argue that fear, as an instinctive response, isn't necessarily a VIRTUE in the way that say, Compassion or Temperance is. If you want to denote &quot;I am a very cautious person who does things carefully&quot; then maybe have Temperance as a Virtue to fluff it as &quot;I do things carefully and deliberately&quot;, while Valor would be &quot;I work through my fear&quot;, as Sunder put it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 05-07-2020, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:11:16-07:00","id":1386528,"title":"","content":"Whatever these Virtues are, I hope they allow you to play an absolute shitheel, a trash fire of a person, a <i>viper.</i><br /> <br /> This without selecting Ambition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T18:04:09-07:00","id":1386572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386521#post1386521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean if you have Compassion as your Major Virtue then I think it would be logical to have a negative Intimacy towards a cruel tyrant that abuses your people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on if having Compassion as a Major Virtue forbids you from having negative Intimacies towards people. But if it doesn't, I agree.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dunno if Fear is needed as one of the big Virtues.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, one could argue that fear, as an instinctive response, isn't necessarily a VIRTUE in the way that say, Compassion or Temperance is. If you want to denote &quot;I am a very cautious person who does things carefully&quot; then maybe have Temperance as a Virtue to fluff it as &quot;I do things carefully and deliberately&quot;, while Valor would be &quot;I work through my fear&quot;, as Sunder put it. </div> </div> </div>Right, fear is a natural response. Often even a healthy one.<br /> <br /> But there's a difference between a passing, cautionary fear, and a chronic, debilitating fear.<br /> <br /> And as you allude, generally speaking, Virtue is about pushing past fear, for any of a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386528#post1386528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever these Virtues are, I hope they allow you to play an absolute shitheel, a trash fire of a person, a <i>viper.</i><br /> <br /> This without selecting Ambition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Valor and Conviction could allow that. Even Temperance only meant you were disciplined and honest, not nice or merciful.<br /> <br /> If Passion/Lust is really a Virtue, it would be completely agnostic to Compassion. You could pursue new experiences and greater heights of pleasure with self-centered, hedonistic abandon.<br /> <br /> <br /> For those passingly familiar with <i>League of Legends</i>, Passion and Valor (in that order) could be the Virtues of Draven, the Glorious Executioner of Noxus. A showboating gladiator and master of the arena, who lives for challenging battles (that he wins) and the adulation of the crowds.<br /> <br /> He is indeed an absolute shitheel, a trash fire of a person, a <i>viper</i>. But still a man driven enough to become a local hero. All without any grand ambitions outside of appeasing his Virtues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T20:41:04-07:00","id":1386604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386572#post1386572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on if having Compassion as a Major Virtue forbids you from having negative Intimacies towards people. But if it doesn't, I agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Compassion says &quot;You cannot ever hate someone no matter how many people they hurt uwu&quot; that's something I'll ignore outright.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hell, even for having Compassion for someone terrible, I'd probably frame it more as &quot;I understand you, even if I can't forgive you, and you're too dangerous to be left unchecked&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T11:49:50-07:00","id":1386751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1385661-the-essence-of-virtue-exalted-essence-s-various-new-categories-of-intimacy?p=1386604#post1386604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Compassion says &quot;You cannot ever hate someone no matter how many people they hurt uwu&quot; that's something I'll ignore outright.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hell, even for having Compassion for someone terrible, I'd probably frame it more as &quot;I understand you, even if I can't forgive you, and you're too dangerous to be left unchecked&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>One can forgive someone and still refuse to trust them.<br /> <br /> One can forgive someone without excusing or forgetting what they did.<br /> <br /> One can forgive someone and still kill them in cold blood because one thinks they're too dangerous to live.<br /> <br /> Forgiveness is merely letting go of hatred.<br /> <br /> One doesn't need to hate someone to kill them. Hating someone is like drinking poison and expecting the other person to die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}